🔹 Program 4: Prefix and Postfix Increment Operator Overloading

📌 Description

This program demonstrates prefix ("++object") and postfix ("object++") increment operator overloading.

In prefix increment, the object is incremented first and the updated object is returned.

In postfix increment, the old value is returned first and then the object is incremented.

🎯 Concept Used

Unary Operator Overloading — Prefix and Postfix Increment

💡 Key Point

A dummy "int" parameter is used to distinguish the postfix increment operator from the prefix increment operator.
